# Key Learning

Long-running background processes should always be managed within the script lifecycle. In this incident, repeated executions of a monitoring 
script continuously spawned `tail -F` processes without terminating them, resulting in orphaned processes accumulating over time. Identifying 
the script design flaw resolved the issue permanently instead of repeatedly killing orphaned processes after each execution.
